{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BufferingResource"}],"platforms":["iOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Expensive interaction with the underlying resource is minimized, since most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(smaller) requests can be satisfied by accessing the buffer alone. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawback is that some extra space is required to hold the buffer and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copying takes place when filling that buffer, but this is usually","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outweighed by the performance benefits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that this implementation is pretty limited and the benefits are only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apparent when reading forward and consecutively – e.g. when downloading the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource by chunks. The buffer is ignored when reading backward or far"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ahead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}],"roleHeading":"Class","title":"BufferingResource","externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared17BufferingResourceC","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BufferingResource","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BufferingResource","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"class"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/bufferingresource"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]}